From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Schaefer <max@excloo.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 18:43:05 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 1056 redfin: use the Android ADSP awake bit

The existing adsp_sleep=1 opt-in publishes the ADSP SMP2P sleepstate entry,
but wrote bit 0 instead of bit 12. Google's Redbull driver defines
PROC_AWAKE_ID 12, sets that bit at probe and after suspend, and clears it
before suspend. The Lito device tree connects its sleepstate consumer to
the ADSP's outbound entry (SMEM 429, inbound 443). Set the existing value to
1u << 12 and make the activation log explicitly report 4096/bit 12.

Keep adsp_sleep unset/0 as the default: master-kernel only. This changes
no SoC metadata, firmware, rails, PMIC writes, sound, microphones, cameras
or thermal protections. SMP2P publication order and doorbell are unchanged.

Provenance (Google immutable Android13 Redbull sources):
https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/msm/+/248fa42a73b230574e84535436c684b3e47a8515/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c
https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/msm-extra/devicetree/+/30211b25c711982716dd2b486bc9b2afe3fe16da/qcom/lito-smp2p.dtsi
https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/msm-extra/devicetree/+/30211b25c711982716dd2b486bc9b2afe3fe16da/qcom/lito.dtsi

The first Redfin sensor trial omitted adsp_sleep, delivered 85 contiguous
accelerometer samples over 3.15 sensor seconds, then reported the public
sar.cc:27:chre_utils fatal signature and lost the DSP. Registry enumeration
had finished earlier. Linux SDM670 bring-up independently reports that
initialising sleepstate prevents the same signature:
https://www.mail-archive.com/linux-remoteproc%40vger.kernel.org/msg00850.html
The wrong awake bit is established by source; this change fixing Redfin's
DSP lifetime remains a hypothesis requiring a fresh controlled off/on
trial with the same pristine served tree, listener and sensor requests.

---
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_adsp.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_adsp.c
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@
 /*
  * 0950: adsp_sleep=1: our SMP2P item carries every entry Android's kernel makes in it (dt: the children of
  * qcom,smp2p-adsp with qcom,smem-state-cells, in order), at Android's boot values: "master-kernel" 0,
- * "sleepstate" 1 (smp2p-sleepstate: bit 0 = APPS awake, set at its probe), "rdbg" 0. adsp_sleep=0 (the
+ * "sleepstate" 4096 (smp2p-sleepstate: bit 12 = APPS awake, set at its probe), "rdbg" 0. adsp_sleep=0 (the
  * default): "master-kernel" only, as before.
  * adsp_qlog=1: every QRTR datagram on IPCRTR (both ways: header and the first 48 bytes) and every intent
  * event of that channel logged, the first 200 lines, then one line per 100 datagrams.
@@ -1692,7 +1692,7 @@
 		static const struct {
 			const char *name;
 			uint32_t value;
-		} more[] = { { "sleepstate", 1 }, { "rdbg", 0 } };
+		} more[] = { { "sleepstate", 1u << 12 }, { "rdbg", 0 } };
 
 		for (unsigned e = 0; e < sizeof(more) / sizeof(more[0]); e++, entries++) {
 			bzero(name, sizeof(name));
@@ -1702,7 +1702,7 @@
 			}
 			smem_poke(our_item + SMP2P_AT_VALUE(entries), more[e].value);
 		}
-		printf("adsp: %u: adsp_sleep=1: our item also has \"sleepstate\" = 1 (APPS awake) and \"rdbg\" = 0, as Android's\n", step);
+		printf("adsp: %u: adsp_sleep=1: our item also has \"sleepstate\" = 4096 (APPS awake bit 12) and \"rdbg\" = 0, as Android's\n", step);
 	}
 	smem_poke(our_item + SMP2P_AT_COUNTS, 16 | entries << 16);
 	smem_poke(our_item + SMP2P_AT_VERSION, SMP2P_RESTART_ACKS << 8);
